Template: netcfg/admin-password
Type: password
Description: Administrator password for the web interface:
 The interface has a single account, named "admin". The password is stored as
 a PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 digest, never in clear text.
 .
 Leave this empty to skip the account for now. netcfg-web is then left stopped
 until you create one by hand.

Template: netcfg/admin-password-again
Type: password
Description: Repeat the administrator password:

Template: netcfg/password-mismatch
Type: error
Description: The two entries do not match
 Enter the same password twice, or leave both empty to skip the account.

Template: netcfg/allow-ssh
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Let the web interface switch the SSH server on and off?
 The interface can open the device's SSH server for a diagnostic window and
 close it again, which is useful on a device you cannot reach any other way.
 .
 It also means anyone who gets into the web interface can open a shell on the
 device, so leave this off unless you need it. Change it later with
 "dpkg-reconfigure netcfg".
